  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 2.0,
    "cls_id": "XF01104",
    "sub_id": "08315",
    "scr_dup": "007",
    "tpa_score_new": "<ol>\n\t<li>midterm interview&nbsp;20%</li>\n\t<li>scantron online final exam20%</li>\n\t<li>course performance 60%\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li>2 Xreading evaluations 15%\n\t\t<ul>\n\t\t\t<li>evaluation 1 7.5% for 30000 wordcounts</li>\n\t\t\t<li>evaluation 2&nbsp;7.5% for 30000 wordcounts</li>\n\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li>in class activities and participation 35%</li>\n\t\t<li>post TOEIC 10%&nbsp;</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": "1. Be on time. 請準時上課。\n2. Participate in the class discussion and class activities. 請參與課堂討論及課堂活動。\n3. Students must submit a leave application to the school in advance, stating the reason for the leave and the expected duration. 如需請假，學生必須提前向學校提交請假申請，說明請假的原因和預計時間。\n4. Please purchase original textbook, following intellectual property law. 請購買正版課本，請勿使用複製版本。\n5. The texts and exercises will be completed in class. Please bring textbooks to class. 請上課攜帶課本，以利上課活動使用。\n6. Follow the school rules to apply for a make-up exam within 14 days of the quiz date. Relevant documents are required for the application. No-shows or those with late application will receive ZERO. The date of a make-up exam will be arranged by the instructor. You are only allowed to apply for a make-up quiz at most 3 times in a semester. Only those who have taken leave on the system can apply. Missing quizzes due to late entry to the classroom or unexcused absence won't be accepted for make-up quiz. 若須要補考小考的同學，請遵照學校的補考規定，在考試後的14天內提出申請。若考試當天沒有出現或者是沒有申請補考的同學，考試成績一律0分。小考一學期至多能申請三次補考，有於系統請假者才可以申請。遲到、曠課一律不接受補考。\n7. No allowance for make-up midterm or/and final exam, unless you have got legitimate and special reason according to the school rules: 期中考和期末考一律不接受補考和補報告，除非為特殊原因或重大事故並：\n(1) Notify the course instructor before the evaluation date 於考試日期前事先告知授課教師\n(2) Need approval from the course instructor in advance 經授課教師事先同意\n(3) Present relevant and official evidence 提出相關正式證明文件\n(4) If something emergent happened, please notify within three days of the exam/evaluation and present relevant and official documents. 如重大事件事發臨時，最晚在考試時間開始三日內告知，並提出相關正式證明文件",
    "course_pol_en": null,
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<ol>\n\t<li>Students must exhibit honesty and ethical behavior in their academic activities, avoiding plagiarism and falsification of data.學生在學術活動中必須展現誠實和道德行為，避免抄襲和篡改資料。</li>\n\t<li>Plagiarism: Proper citation of sources is required. Copying or using others&#39; work without appropriate attribution is considered plagiarism.抄襲：必須適當引用來源。未經適當標示使用他人作品屬於抄襲行為。</li>\n\t<li>Cheating: Following exam rules is mandatory. Unauthorized materials or collusion with others during exams is considered cheating.考試作弊：必須遵守考試規則，禁止使用未經授權的材料或與他人串通作弊。</li>\n</ol>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": null,
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
